# Context file rules

## Never invent product facts

Do not fill any placeholder with assumed or inferred product behavior. If the answer is unknown, write `[OPEN]` and leave it for the discovery workflow. A placeholder left blank is better than a confident guess.

## Status labels — use them on every non-trivial claim

| Label | When to use |
|-------|------------|
| `[DECIDED]` | Agreed by the team, reflected in spec |
| `[IMPLEMENTED]` | Code already matches this |
| `[HYPOTHESIS]` | Reasonable bet, not yet validated |
| `[OPEN]` | Unresolved — needs a decision before building |
| `[FUTURE]` | Intentionally out of v1 scope |

## Cross-file consistency — check before saving

When any of these sections change, verify the listed files stay aligned:

| Changed section | Check these too |
|----------------|----------------|
| Overview or Goals | Features, Scope, Success Criteria (same file) |
| Core User Flow | `architecture.md` system boundaries |
| Features or Scope | `progress-tracker.md` next steps and open questions |
| Stack or storage model | `architecture.md` invariants |
| Any decision that contradicts code | Add a note: `Code: [current] → Spec: [intended]` |

## When a section changes

1. Update upstream sections first (Overview → Goals → Flow → Scope).
2. Add deferred decisions to `progress-tracker.md` under Open Questions.
3. Do not silently rewrite — show the proposed change and confirm before saving.

## `progress-tracker.md` must stay current

After any meaningful change to any context file, `progress-tracker.md` must reflect:
- What was decided
- What is now open or deferred
- What the code does not yet match
